{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NoncommRing","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.TwoSidedIdeal.Kernel","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TemperleyLiebAlgebra"],"declarations":40,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.tlRelator_mem_ker","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.tlRelator_mem_ker","kind":"theorem","line":564,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L564-L584","doc":"**The Temperley–Lieb relator lies in the kernel.**\n\n`U_i := T_i + 1` maps to `u_i = v·e_i`, and the extra relation cutting `TL` out\nof `H` is `U_i U_j U_i = q·U_i` for adjacent `i, j` — which in `H` is a genuine\nrelation only modulo the ideal. This exhibits that relator as an explicit\nelement of `tlKernel`, so the ideal is not merely named: it visibly contains\nwhat it is supposed to contain.\n\nIt does **not** show the relators generate it. That is the `⊆` half of the open\nquestion below, and the easier half. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.tlKernel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.tlKernel","kind":"def","line":550,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L550-L562","doc":"**The Temperley–Lieb ideal** — the kernel of the quotient map, as a\ntwo-sided ideal.\n\n`TwoSidedIdeal`, not `Ideal`: Mathlib's `Ideal` is `Submodule R R` and is the\n*commutative* notion, while `HeckeAlgebra` is not commutative. That distinction\nis why the first-isomorphism step below is stated as an open engineering item\nrather than proved.\n\nThis is a definition and asserts nothing about what the ideal is. It exists so\nthat the open question can be *written down*. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.heckeTLEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.heckeTLEquiv","kind":"def","line":508,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L508-L539","doc":"**`TL_n(δ) ≅ H_n(v²) / ⟨U_i U_j U_i − v²·U_i⟩`**, as `R`-algebras.\n\nThe presentation-level Temperley–Lieb theorem: `TL` is `H` with exactly one\nextra family of relations imposed. Stronger than \"quotient by the kernel\",\nbecause the ideal is *named by generators* rather than merely named.\n\nBoth round trips are `hom_ext` checks on generators: `e_i ↦ w·U_i ↦ w·u_i = e_i`\none way, and `mk(T_i) ↦ u_i − 1 ↦ mk(U_i) − 1 = mk(T_i)` the other. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.tlToQuot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.tlToQuot","kind":"def","line":481,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L481-L506","doc":"**Backward map** `TL → H/⟨relators⟩`, `e_i ↦ w·U_i`.\n\nEach of the three Temperley–Lieb relations is checked: the loop relation from\n`U_sq` (which holds in `H` before quotienting), the adjacency relation from the\nrelator (the one place the quotient is used), and commutation from `U_comm`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.quotToTL_mkTL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.quotToTL_mkTL","kind":"theorem","line":460,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L460-L464","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.quotToTL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.quotToTL","kind":"def","line":448,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L448-L458","doc":"**Forward map** `H/⟨relators⟩ → TL`. Well-defined because `heckeToTL`\nidentifies the two sides of each relator — which is `u_adj`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.heckeToTL_U","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.heckeToTL_U","kind":"theorem","line":442,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L442-L446","doc":"`heckeToTL` sends `U_i = T_i + 1` to `u_i = v·e_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.heckeTL_hom_ext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.heckeTL_hom_ext","kind":"theorem","line":422,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L422-L433","doc":"**Uniqueness of maps out of the quotient.** `mkTL` is surjective and `H` has\n`hom_ext`, so agreement on the images of the Hecke generators suffices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.mkTL_rel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.mkTL_rel","kind":"theorem","line":416,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L416-L420","doc":"**The relator holds downstairs**, by construction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.mkTL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.mkTL","kind":"def","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L410-L412","doc":"The quotient map `H ↠ H/⟨relators⟩`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.instAlgebraHeckeTL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.instAlgebraHeckeTL","kind":"instance","line":407,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L407-L408","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.instRingHeckeTL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.instRingHeckeTL","kind":"instance","line":404,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L404-L405","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.HeckeTL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.HeckeTL","kind":"def","line":401,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L401-L402","doc":"**`H_n(q)` modulo the Temperley–Lieb relators.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.TLRel.adj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.TLRel.adj","kind":"ctor","line":397,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L397-L399","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.TLRel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.TLRel","kind":"inductive","line":394,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L394-L399","doc":"**The Temperley–Lieb relator**, as a relation on `H`: `U_i U_j U_i = q·U_i`\nfor adjacent `i, j`. This is the *entire* difference between the two algebras. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.U_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.U_comm","kind":"theorem","line":385,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L385-L390","doc":"…hence so do the `U_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.T_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.T_comm","kind":"theorem","line":376,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L376-L383","doc":"Non-adjacent Hecke generators commute — the braid relation at `M i j = 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.U_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.U_sq","kind":"theorem","line":359,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L359-L372","doc":"**`U_i² = q·U_i + U_i` holds in `H` already** — it is the Iwahori quadratic\nrelation rearranged, not an imposed relation. This is why the loop relation\ntransports without the quotient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.U","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.U","kind":"def","line":353,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L353-L355","doc":"**`U_i := T_i + 1`.** The Iwahori-normalised Temperley–Lieb generator: it is\n`U_i² = (q+1)·U_i` on the nose in `H`, before any quotient. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.isTypeADiagram_coxeterFin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.isTypeADiagram_coxeterFin","kind":"theorem","line":318,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L318-L328","doc":"**The hypothesis is inhabited.** So the surjection theorem is a statement\nabout a nonempty class, not a vacuous implication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.coxeterFin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.coxeterFin","kind":"def","line":313,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L313-L316","doc":"The type-A Coxeter matrix of the linear diagram on `Fin n`: `1` on the\ndiagonal, `3` on adjacent pairs, `2` elsewhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.heckeToTL_surjective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.heckeToTL_surjective","kind":"theorem","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L274-L298","doc":"**The map is surjective**, given a right inverse `w` for `v`.\n\n`v` must be a unit and this is the one place it is needed: `e_i` is recovered as\n`w · (T_i + 1)`, so without an inverse for `v` the generators need not be in the\nimage at all. Everything above holds over any commutative ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.adjoin_range_e_eq_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.adjoin_range_e_eq_top","kind":"theorem","line":250,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L250-L270","doc":"**`TL` is generated by its `e_i`.**\n\n`RingQuot.mkAlgHom` is surjective and `FreeAlgebra` is generated by `ι`, so the\nimage of the generators generates. Stated here rather than in\n`TemperleyLiebAlgebra` only because that is where it was first needed; it is a\nfact about the presentation, not about this map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.heckeToTL_T","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.heckeToTL_T","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L238-L240","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.heckeToTL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.heckeToTL","kind":"def","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L216-L236","doc":"**The Temperley–Lieb quotient map** `H_n(v²) →ₐ[R] TL_n(δ)`, `T_i ↦ v·e_i − 1`.\n\nBuilt by `IwahoriHecke.lift`, so the two obligations are exactly the Hecke\nrelations, discharged by `quadratic_of_sq` and `braid3_of` / `commute_of`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.u_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.u_comm","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L201-L205","doc":"**Non-adjacent `u`'s commute**, inherited from `e_farCommute`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.u_adj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.u_adj","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L189-L199","doc":"**The adjacency relation on `u`**: `u_i u_j u_i = q·u_i` with `q = v²`.\n\nNo hypothesis on `δ` is needed — the `v³` on the left meets `v² · v` on the\nright. That is the abstract lemma's \"`Q` cancels\" made concrete. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.u_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.u_sq","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L177-L187","doc":"**The loop relation on `u`**: `u_i² = q·u_i + u_i`, with `q = v²`.\n\nThis is the only place `v·δ = v² + 1` is used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.e_sq_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.e_sq_smul","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L172-L175","doc":"`e_i² = δ • e_i`, the loop relation in `•` form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.u","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.u","kind":"def","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L162-L168","doc":"**The rescaled Temperley–Lieb generator** `u_i = v · e_i`.\n\nRescaling by `v` moves the loop parameter from `δ` to `v·δ = v² + 1 = q + 1`, the\nIwahori-normalised value, and moves the adjacency relation from\n`e_i e_j e_i = e_i` to `u_i u_j u_i = q·u_i`. Those two shifts are exactly what\nreconciles the two files' conventions; see the header. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.commute_of","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.commute_of","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L137-L143","doc":"**Commutation is inherited by the shift.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.braid3_of","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.braid3_of","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L116-L135","doc":"**The length-3 braid relation, abstractly.**\n\nGiven the loop relation for each of `u₁, u₂` and the two adjacency relations\n`u₁u₂u₁ = Q·u₁`, `u₂u₁u₂ = Q·u₂`, the shifted elements `u − 1` braid.\n\n**`Q` cancels.** Both sides reduce to `−u₁u₂ − u₂u₁ + u₁ + u₂ − 1`, so the\nidentity holds for *any* `Q` satisfying those hypotheses, with no centrality and\nno relation between `Q` and a loop parameter. That is why the substitution works\nat all: the braid relation is not an extra constraint on `δ` once the loop\nrelation is imposed on the rescaled generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.quadratic_of_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.quadratic_of_sq","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L103-L114","doc":"**The Iwahori quadratic relation, abstractly.**\n\nIf `u * u = Q * u + u` then `x := u − 1` satisfies `(x − Q)(x + 1) = 0`.\n\nNo hypothesis on `Q` at all — not centrality, not invertibility. The relation is\n`(u − 1 − Q) * u = u*u − u − Q*u`, and the assumption is exactly what makes that\nvanish. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.IsTypeADiagram.adj_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.IsTypeADiagram.adj_symm","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L95-L95","doc":"Adjacency is symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.IsTypeADiagram.adj_irrefl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.IsTypeADiagram.adj_irrefl","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L93-L93","doc":"Adjacency is irreflexive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.IsTypeADiagram.far","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.IsTypeADiagram.far","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L91-L91","doc":"Distinct non-adjacent generators commute. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.IsTypeADiagram.adj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.IsTypeADiagram.adj","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L89-L89","doc":"Adjacent generators satisfy the length-3 braid relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.IsTypeADiagram.diag","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.IsTypeADiagram.diag","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L87-L87","doc":"`M i i = 1`: a generator braids trivially with itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.IsTypeADiagram.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.IsTypeADiagram.mk","kind":"ctor","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L85-L85","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.IsTypeADiagram","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeToTemperleyLieb.IsTypeADiagram","kind":"structure","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/HeckeToTemperleyLieb.lean#L75-L95","doc":"**Type-A compatibility between a Coxeter matrix and an adjacency predicate.**\n\n`IwahoriHecke` is indexed by a Coxeter matrix `M`; `TemperleyLieb` by an\nadjacency predicate `Adj`. This says they describe the same diagram: `3` on\nadjacent pairs (the braid relation), `2` on distinct non-adjacent ones\n(commutation), `1` on the diagonal.\n\nA structure rather than four loose hypotheses because all of them are needed\ntogether at every use, and because `adj_irrefl` is the one that is easy to\nforget — without it `M i i` would have to be both `1` and `3`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}